            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0275" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg181"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.348 Z 4/169: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Robbins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-10-02T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 2,
                                1924—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 2—2:54
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>200. Embassy’s 188, September 10, 3 p.m.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d150-f1"/> Foreign
                    Office now states informally that presumably Zeppelin will fly to the United
                    States under German flag and that consequently German authorities should procure
                    necessary permissions for flight over foreign territories. In reply to verbal
                    inquiry the Embassy has informally expressed concurrence in the foregoing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robbins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
